      "problem": "Evaluate${\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(2i-1)=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $i$ from $1$ to $3.$ So, computing the terms for $i=1,2,3$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}(2i-1) & =(2(1)-1)+(2(2)-1)+(2(3)-1) \\\\  & =(2-1)+(4-1)+(6-1) \\\\  & =1+3+5 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
